SUMMARY:Careless People by Sarah Wynn-Williams
DESCRIPTION:Petaluma Book (And Brew) Club\nPLEASE NOTE THE LIBRARY HOLD SY
 STEM FOR PHYSICAL BOOKS IS CLOSED WHILE THEY UPDATE THE SYSTEM\n\nSarah Wy
 nn-Williams joined Facebook believing the company could change things for 
 the better. Instead\, what she encountered over seven years was so shockin
 g that Meta obtained a legal order to silence her.\n\nNow you can read her
  award-winning story. Candid and entertaining\, Wynn-Williams’ account p
 ulls back the curtain on Mark Zuckerberg\, Sheryl Sandberg and the global 
 elite. She exposes the true cost of Silicon Valley’s ambition\, from out
 rageous schemes cooked up on private jets to the alarming consequences of 
 Facebook’s aggressive pursuit of global dominance.\n\nCareless People is
  an ordinary woman's gripping and darkly funny memoir that will forever ch
 ange how you view the technology that runs our lives – and the unchecked
  power of those who control it.
